      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure about the performance impact here, see: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/947417/comment/1097e8df_db19f201/\n\nWe might need to ask Lorenzo if he knows more details. IIUC this will be called every time a service is resolved or updated.\n\nMaybe there\u0027s no way to cache this, since the ordering can change when interface configuration or routes changes ? But it also shows another problem: if the interface config changes, and should affect the ordering, the MdnsServiceInfo is out-of-date (it uses old ordering), but we won\u0027t send a SERVICE_UPDATED callback at that time. It would be nice to clarify in which case the ordering will change.\n\nSo I think we need to know:\n - When can the source address for a given destination address change\n - How costly is it to run the current code on every address, on every service update\n - Is there any way to cache it, if we can predict when the source address can change (cache should be cleared) ?\n - If we can predict when the source address can change and the ordering change, should we send SERVICE_UPDATED at that time ?",
